[38.133735, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThis is primarily a \u001b[1mmanifest problem\u001b[0m. The \u001b[1;36;40mml-scorer\u001b[0m pod's resource requests (\u001b[1;36;40m64 CPU\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40m512Gi\u001b[0m       \r\r\nmemory) are unrealistically high and far exceed the capacity of any node in the cluster.            \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mKey Points:\u001b[0m                                                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCluster Capacity\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mEach node has \u001b[1;36;40m20 CPU\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40m31.0Gi\u001b[0m memory allocatable.                                           \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThese are reasonable resource limits for typical workloads, but the pod's requests are over 3x\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mthe CPU and over 16x the memory of a single node.                                             \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mManifest Problem\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe pod's resource requests are misconfigured in the deployment manifest. Such high resource  \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mrequests are unlikely to be intentional unless the workload genuinely requires them (e.g.,    "]
[38.166702, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KThis is primarily a \u001b[1mmanifest problem\u001b[0m. The \u001b[1;36;40mml-scorer\u001b[0m pod's resource requests (\u001b[1;36;40m64 CPU\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40m512Gi\u001b[0m       \r\r\nmemory) are unrealistically high and far exceed the capacity of any node in the cluster.            \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mKey Points:\u001b[0m                                                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCluster Capacity\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mEach node has \u001b[1;36;40m20 CPU\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40m31.0Gi\u001b[0m memory allocatable.                                           \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThese are reasonable resource limits for typical workloads, but the pod's requests are over 3x\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mthe CPU and over 16x the memory of a single node.                                             \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mManifest Problem\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe pod's resource requests are misconfigured in the deployment manifest. Such high resource  \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mrequests are unlikely to be intentional unless the workload genuinely requires them (e.g.,    \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mhigh-performance computing or large-scale machine learning).                                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mConclusion:\u001b[0m                                                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\nThe root cause is the manifest's resource requests, not the cluster's capacity. Fixing the manifest \r\r\nto request realistic resources (e.g., \u001b[1;36;40m2 CPU\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40m2Gi\u001b[0m memory) will resolve the issue without requiring\r\r\ncluster scaling.                                                                                    \r\r\n\r\r\nWould you like me to patch the deployment to correct the resource requests?                         \r\r\n\u001b[?25h"]
